>> title: Chicken Parmigiana
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: chicken, breaded, tomato, mozzarella, italian, fried, oven
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: chicken parm, chicken parmesan, chicken parmigiano, parm, parmigiana, pollo alla parmigiana
>> pairs-with: marinara-sauce, fresh-egg-pasta
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — the sauce goes down the middle only; sauce to the edges softens the crust under the oven and a wet crumb never crisps back

Preheat the #oven{} to 425°F (220°C) ~preheat{15%min}.

>> step: pound to 1/4 in and salt
Pound @chicken breasts{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; halved horizontally into four cutlets) to 1/4 in between two sheets of plastic, salt them with @kosher salt{2%tsp}, and ~rest{20%min}.

>> step: dredge flour, egg, then crumb
Dredge @&(~1)cutlets{} through @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(60 g), then @eggs{2%large}(100 g; beaten), then @dried breadcrumbs{1 1/2%cup}(160 g) tossed with @grated parmesan{1/2%cup}(50 g) and @dried oregano{1%tsp}, pressing the crumb on and shaking the loose flour off first.

>> step: fry 3 min a side, drain on a rack
Fry @&(~1)breaded cutlets{} two at a time in @neutral oil{1%cup}(240 mL) at 350°F (175°C) ~fry{6%min}, turning once, and drain them on a rack rather than on paper, which steams the underside soft.

>> step: spoon the sauce down the middle only
Top @&(~1)fried cutlets{} in a #baking dish{} with @marinara sauce{2%cup}(480 mL; from the recipe on this shelf) spooned down the middle of each and nowhere near the edges, then @low-moisture mozzarella{8%oz}(225 g; sliced).

>> step: bake 425°F (220°C) 12 min, until it blisters
Bake @&(~1)dish{} on the top rack ~bake{12%min}, until the cheese has blistered and slumped over the sides.

Parm is a method rather than a bird: veal eggplant meatballs and butterflied shrimp all go the same way.
